The attached image presents flow cytometry histograms showing the expression of co-stimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs). The gray line represents control DCs incubated with medium, while the black line represents DCs treated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 for two days. As per the context from the PDF's Figure 6, Nano-11 significantly enhanced the expression of CD80 and CD86, with a slight increase in CD40, on DCs. This indicates that Nano-11 activates DCs, a crucial step in initiating an effective adaptive immune response.